607 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (      This report covers the design cycle of an autonomous pet-feeding robot. The robot fills a  preprogrammed number of bowls with an associated amount of food, aiming to reduce the need to manually fill pet bowls and prevent pet health issues. The system features a VEX based mechanical chassis and 3D printed structures. It navigates through its environment using sensor inputs, which control the conditions of the motors. To account for more than one bowl and the possibility of an obstacle, a for-loop programmed to loop for the number of bowls was utilized to repeat the food dispensing action only when a bowl was detected. Motor encoders allow for the robot to return to original position after task completion. The final robot successfully completed its tasks, however, issues such as misalignment during navigation, jammed food, and food spillage caused by robot movement and vibration made it impractical for real-world use. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
