645 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (      The robot will move throughout its environment in order to complete its tasks. It will utilize two motors attached to the front wheels to drive forward beside the bowls, stop when an object is detected by the bumper sensor, and drive backwards to its starting position when it has completed its task. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
646 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (       One motor will be used to control how much food is dispensed into the bowl. The motor will be attached to a bar-like structure, initially positioned to keep the trapdoor for the food container closed. Once the robot is aligned with the food bowl and the colour has been detected, the motor will activate and move the bar away from the trapdoor, allowing food to flow out. The motor will only move the bar away for the preprogrammed amount of time that corresponds with the colour of the bowl detected by the optical sensor. Once the time runs out, the motor will move the bar back into its initial position, closing the trapdoor and not allowing any more food to flow out. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
647 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (      One motor will be used to control the raising and lowering of the lever arm containing the bumper sensor. The robot initially starts with the lever arm upright to save space. Once the Touch LED is pressed, the motor attached to the lever arm will rotate 90 degrees so that the arm is parallel with the ground. As the robot drives forward and the bumper comes into contact with an object, the robot will either dispense the pet food or move past the object depending on the colour detected. Afterwards, the motor rotates to its initial orientation, raising the lever arm back to its upright position. This position is kept while the robot drives forward until the colour of the object is no longer detected. Then, the motor will again turn 90 degrees for the lever arm to be parallel to the ground and the process is repeated until all bowls are filled. Once the robot has completed its task, the motor raises the bumper arm to its upright position before traveling back to its starting location to prevent the arm from hitting any objects on the way back. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [13 14]
>>
endobj
