662 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (      For the first constraint, the bowls must be aligned within a defined area so that when the robot travels in a straight line, it remains approximately 3-5 inches away from the bowl. This allows the lever arm with the bumper sensor on the robot to reliably reach the bowl to signal to the robot when to stop and dispense the food \(when the bumper presses against the bowl, and the colour sensor detects the colour of the bowl\).)
/E (      For the first constraint, the bowls must be aligned within a defined area so that when the robot travels in a straight line, it remains approximately 3-5 inches away from the bowl. This allows the lever arm with the bumper sensor on the robot to reliably reach the bowl to signal to the robot when to stop and dispense the food \(when the bumper presses against the bowl, and the colour sensor detects the colour of the bowl\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
663 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (      Changes: This constraint was added after our informal presentation. Previously, the design did not feature a lever arm and instead had a self-aligning mechanism on the front to guide the robot. This was since changed to feature the new lever arm design. Hence, this constraint was added. Additionally, it must be contained within this area so that the colour sensor can accurately sense the hue of the robot so it dispenses the right amount of food.)
/E (      Changes: This constraint was added after our informal presentation. Previously, the design did not feature a lever arm and instead had a self-aligning mechanism on the front to guide the robot. This was since changed to feature the new lever arm design. Hence, this constraint was added. Additionally, it must be contained within this area so that the colour sensor can accurately sense the hue of the robot so it dispenses the right amount of food.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
