668 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (      Another constraint is that the robot must be compact enough to be easily stored in a home environment. This is important for aesthetic purposes in a home. To address this constraint, the code was modified so that the lever arm lifts up to be positioned perpendicular to the ground before returning to its home position. This ensures that the robot can be compactly stored in the users designated storage spot. Lifting the lever arm ensures that the robot can fit within a 1.5ft x 1.5ft x 1.5ft dimension. The team also prioritized a compact form by incorporating an easily removable food container, giving the user the option to store the container separately. )
/E (      Another constraint is that the robot must be compact enough to be easily stored in a home environment. This is important for aesthetic purposes in a home. To address this constraint, the code was modified so that the lever arm lifts up to be positioned perpendicular to the ground before returning to its home position. This ensures that the robot can be compactly stored in the users designated storage spot. Lifting the lever arm ensures that the robot can fit within a 1.5ft x 1.5ft x 1.5ft dimension. The team also prioritized a compact form by incorporating an easily removable food container, giving the user the option to store the container separately. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10 11]
>>
endobj
