686 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (      The design of the robot utilizes a chassis and motor drive system similar to the original configuration of the robot, a lever arm, a container holder and base, and a trapdoor mechanism. It also features the bumper, optical, and touch sensor. The design of this robot prioritizes simplicity in its design to streamline 3D printing, uncomplex mechanisms and features to simplify the code needed to run them, and an unobtrusive perimeter to allow the robot to be out of the way when not in use. The final design utilized the VEX Lego parts, and SolidWorks to design the custom pieces which were 3D printed in PLA.)
/E (      The design of the robot utilizes a chassis and motor drive system similar to the original configuration of the robot, a lever arm, a container holder and base, and a trapdoor mechanism. It also features the bumper, optical, and touch sensor. The design of this robot prioritizes simplicity in its design to streamline 3D printing, uncomplex mechanisms and features to simplify the code needed to run them, and an unobtrusive perimeter to allow the robot to be out of the way when not in use. The final design utilized the VEX Lego parts, and SolidWorks to design the custom pieces which were 3D printed in PLA.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [6 7]
>>
endobj
