700 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (      The sensors used in this robot were the bumper, optical, and touch sensor. The bumper was attached to the end of the lever arm as stated in the previous subsection. The optical sensor was placed on the left side of the robot facing where the slide and trapdoor will open to. It was attached low on the chassis in between the wheels so it would be low enough to read the colour of the dog bowls, and in line with the slide so when the robot stops to deposit the food, the sensor can read the colour. The touch sensor was placed on the right side of the robot, under the supports for the food container. The touch sensor needed to be placed somewhere easy to reach so it was on the outer edge of the perimeter without anything in the way.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
