709 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (      The trapdoor was the most heavily reiterated mechanism. Throughout the design process, its placement, mechanics, and resting orientation was edited continuously until a design was found that upheld all the most important needs and restrictions. Initially, the trapdoor was positioned on the bottom of the container, which would allow for gravity to push the food out when the door slid out of place. Then, the trapdoor was positioned facing the front of the robot with a slide to bring the food to the bowls, because the way the robot approached the bowls changed to pulling up in front of them. This iteration had the trapdoor hinge open using a motor shaft as the pin of the hinge to motorize the door open and closed. This design had some flaws in the use of the motorized hinge, as it was hard to orient the motor against the container holder in a way that it did not interfere with the holder while still being close enough to sit within the hinge. Once the incline was added to the container holder, a new solution for the trapdoor emerged using gravity to its advantage. )
/E (      The trapdoor was the most heavily reiterated mechanism. Throughout the design process, its placement, mechanics, and resting orientation was edited continuously until a design was found that upheld all the most important needs and restrictions. Initially, the trapdoor was positioned on the bottom of the container, which would allow for gravity to push the food out when the door slid out of place. Then, the trapdoor was positioned facing the front of the robot with a slide to bring the food to the bowls, because the way the robot approached the bowls changed to pulling up in front of them. This iteration had the trapdoor hinge open using a motor shaft as the pin of the hinge to motorize the door open and closed. This design had some flaws in the use of the motorized hinge, as it was hard to orient the motor against the container holder in a way that it did not interfere with the holder while still being close enough to sit within the hinge. Once the incline was added to the container holder, a new solution for the trapdoor emerged using gravity to its advantage. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
