/E (      Due to mechanical errors, some constraints had to be removed and some had to be modified for the final demo in order to be met.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
944 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (      The first constraint listed on the previous page was that the bowls must be aligned collinear to each other so that the robot would drive in a straight line, 3-5 inches away from the bowls horizontally. However, the robot did not always move in a perfectly straight line due to uneven surfaces and the motion of the lever arm causing the robot to slightly deviate from its trajectory. To address this issue, our team had to ensure that the bowls are in the correct path of the robot by moving them around instead of having them fixed in straight line, since the robot did not always move in a straight path. The bowls had to be manually moved so that it lined up to be 3-5 inches away from the robot.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
945 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (      A criteria that was not fully met during the demo was that the robot had to accurately detect the hue of the bowl, and if it detected something other than the bowl, consider it an obstacle and move on in order to find either of the bowls. During the demo, however, the robot occasionally detected the bowls as an obstacle, due to the colour sensor not correctly detecting the hue of the bowls. This did not meet one of the criteria, which was to dispense food depending on the bowl colour, and since the correct bowl colour was not detected, the robot did not dispense the food. To address this issue, the bowl had to be moved during the demo so that it could be redetected as the robot continued on its path, until it properly sensed the bowl again. To fix this issue for future trials, the hue tolerance can be increased in the code for the robot, and the trials should be done in a brighter lighting so the colour of the bowls are accurately sensed.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
946 0 obj
<<
